{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789214494,"nonce":"0DJCvHTFTdMW8U57+tWaE0TaAEw=","title":"Immix as the pluggable collector for dynamic languages, cooperating with the drop analysis","message":"MemoryStrategy already names Hybrid, and the design intent is that\nmemory management is a menu the embedding language picks from:\ndrop-site analysis by default, a collector opt-in. Python is the first\nlanguage that needs the collector, because most of its values are Any\nand most Any lifetimes are unprovable.\n\nThe collector is Immix, non-moving to start (sticky). Two sibling\nimplementations exist. brass/stickyimmix is a 1.2k-line heap skeleton\nwith the right shape (block allocator, line marks, bump into holes,\ngeneric over the object header) and no collector: its mark is a stub.\ncaribou/heap/immix.rs is a 6k-line complete collector (mark, line\nsweep, large and immortal spaces, root registration, conservative\nscan ranges) but is wired to HashLink's object model and cannot be\nlinked. So: the skeleton from the first, the algorithm from the\nsecond, in a Zyntax runtime crate with a C ABI the backends call.\n\n\nAsh's escape pass measured 52% of a program in the collector before\nrouting non-escaping allocations around it. Zyntax already has the\nanalysis that decides this: drop_insert classifies every allocation as\nproven (SingleBlockDrop, MultiBlockDrop) or not (Escaped, MultiBlock).\nToday unproven means leak or manual free. Under Hybrid, unproven means\ntraced.\n\n1. Allocation routing. A proven site keeps Intrinsic::Malloc and its\n   inserted free, from the pool as now. An unproven site is rewritten\n   to a new Intrinsic::GcAlloc and is the collector's. The pass that\n   already knows which is which does the rewrite. Nothing the static\n   analysis can prove ever enters the heap.\n\n2. Trace glue from drop glue. drop_glue synthesises a per-type release\n   that knows exactly which fields are pointers. That field walk is\n   what a tracer is. The same synthesis emits `__trace__T(obj, visit)`\n   for GC-allocated types; for an owned type the walk ends in a free,\n   for a traced type it ends in the visitor. One layout source, two\n   consumers, so they cannot disagree about offsets.\n\n3. Soundness across the two heaps, both directions. An owned object\n   holding a GC pointer would hide a root from the collector, so a type\n   with any GC-typed field is itself GC-allocated (taint propagates\n   through the type). A GC object holding an owned pointer would keep\n   reading it after the owner's proven free, but storing a pointer into\n   another object is already an Escape in drop_insert, so such a site\n   is unproven and goes to the GC anyway. No new rule is needed for the\n   second direction; the first is one check at type-classification.\n\n4. Roots. Conservative stack scanning first (caribou's add_scan_range\n   shape), which sticky Immix makes safe because nothing moves. The\n   drop analysis's liveness is a precise stack map waiting to be\n   emitted; that is the upgrade path to evacuation. Fiber frames and\n   handler state are roots and register as such; per-fiber handler\n   stacks already know their extent.\n\n5. DynamicBox. Boxed Any values are malloc'd and released by\n   drop_insert through zyntax_box_free today. Under Hybrid, a box whose\n   lifetime is unproven is GC-allocated with a header, and box_free on\n   a GC box is a no-op. This is the common case for Python.\n\n6. Selection. The embedding language sets the strategy; ZynML stays on\n   the ownership default and pays nothing. The intrinsic split means a\n   backend with no collector linked compiles GcAlloc to Malloc and the\n   program leaks rather than faults, which is the right degradation.\n\n\n(a) runtime crate: blocks, lines, bump alloc, mark bits, line sweep,\nlarge objects, conservative roots; C ABI gc_alloc/gc_collect/gc_root.\n(b) Intrinsic::GcAlloc through all four backends, falling back to\nMalloc where no collector is linked.\n(c) drop_insert rewrites unproven sites under Hybrid; taint check.\n(d) drop_glue emits trace glue alongside release glue.\n(e) roots from fibers and handler state.\n(f) measure on the Python subset with and without (c): the number to\nwatch is time in the collector, which Ash put at 52% before routing.","files":null}]}